# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# Supplied source asset tree (~120MB of FBX/OBJ/STL/PNG plus their renders).
# These are inputs, not source code, and are far past the size where committing
# them is sensible. `npm run assets` reads from here to populate public/assets.
#
# This tree is macOS-only to process: prepare-assets.sh shells out to `sips` and
# `cwebp`, which are Apple binaries. The optimised output below is what ships.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. An unanchored `assets/` also matches
# `public/assets/`, which is the runtime payload the deployment needs — ignoring
# it produces a site that builds cleanly and then has no models and no video.
/assets/

# NOTE: public/assets/ is deliberately NOT ignored, unlike the source tree
# above. It is generated locally (the pipeline cannot run on Vercel's Linux
# builders) and is therefore the only copy that reaches the deployment, so it
# has to live in version control. It is ~23MB, dominated by the 13MB intro
# sting. Regenerate with `npm run assets` after changing the source assets.

# Local agent tooling, not part of the project
.agents/
skills-lock.json

